  "paragraphs": [
    [
      "The student council wanted to choose a new lunchtime activity.",
      "Ari made a survey and asked students near the sports field to reply.",
      "Of the 30 replies, 26 suggested football and four suggested music."
    ],
    [
      "Ari counted the answers carefully.",
      "A clear majority had chosen football.",
      "He was ready to tell the council that almost everyone in the school wanted it."
    ],
    [
      "However, his friend noticed that all the replies came from the same place.",
      "Students who spent lunchtime in the library had not been asked.",
      "The count was correct, but the survey was not representative of the whole school."
    ],
    [
      "The next day, Ari collected replies in several other places.",
      "The new results included more suggestions for art and music.",
      "He still reported the first results, but explained who had answered.",
      "A large number of similar answers was useful only when he understood whose voices were missing."
    ]
  ],
  "translations": [
    "学生会想选择一种新的午间活动。",
    "阿里做了一份调查，请运动场附近的学生回答。",
    "30 份回复中，26 份建议足球，4 份建议音乐。",
    "阿里仔细数了答案。",
    "明显的多数选择了足球。",
    "他准备告诉学生会，学校里几乎每个人都想选足球。",
    "然而，朋友注意到，所有回复都来自同一个地方。",
    "在图书馆度过午间时间的学生并没有被询问。",
    "计数正确，但调查不能代表全校。",
    "第二天，阿里又在其他几个地方收集了回复。",
    "新结果里出现了更多美术和音乐方面的建议。",
    "他仍报告了最初的结果，但解释了是谁作答的。",
    "只有弄清哪些人的声音缺失了，大量相似答案才对他有用。"
  ],
